DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Interval");
Context()->operators->undefine('+','-','*','/');
$set_ans_1 = Compute("{2, 8, 13, 18} - ((-infinity, infinity) - (1, infinity)) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (1, infinity))");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("({2, 8, 13, 18}) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {2, 8, 13, 18}) U {2, 8, 13, 18} U (1, infinity)");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("(((1, infinity) U {2, 8, 13, 18} U (({2, 8, 13, 18} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {2, 8, 13, 18})))) U {2, 8, 13, 18}) U {2, 8, 13, 18}");
BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{2, 8, 13, 18\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x > 0\}`]

Compute:
- [`A \cap B \cap B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`(A) \cap A \cup A \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`((B \cup A \cup ((A \cap A))) \cup A) \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

[`1+14-16-1`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>Real(-2),width=>1}
---

What is the value of [`17+4-3/6`]? [_____]{answer=>Formula("20.5"),width=>7}
---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
